 @chrono_tigger  In regards to dual GPU, bridging two cards together to work as "one" isn't a feature I use.
All applications I run on my cards doesn't require a bridge, since each card is used independently from the other. (they still work on the same task, but doesn't have to speak to each other.) So I can slot in 10+ cards if the motherboard has room for it. (And no, it isn't crypto mining, though second hand mining GPUs are still on my radar, if the price drops low enough. Though, then I'll stuff them into my server....)

In regards to the "1650", of course one goes for the 1650 super, though, I buy most stuff second hand, so if I get a 1650 for 35% cheaper, it is still a good deal.

